    // could land a replacement character inside the needle.
    //
    // Matched as the SECOND line, whole — not "somewhere in the prefix"
    // (E-21): line 1 is the shebang and line 2 is the marker, both emitted
    // before any interpolated (and therefore attacker/operator-influenced)
    // value, so a baked `$OCX_HOME` that happens to spell the marker can
    // never land there. `nth(1)` is `None` on a `\n`-free prefix, so a short
    // read answers `false` with no special case, and no line 2 can arrive
    // truncated: the marker sits at bytes 10..36 of a 256-byte window.
    prefix
        .split(|byte| *byte == b'\n')
        .nth(1)
        .is_some_and(|line| line == TRAMPOLINE_MARKER.as_bytes())
